 {r}←LogError msg
⍝ Uses Plodder's `AppLogError`, the official function for logging application errors: it
⍝ enforces the format by putting "*** Error" in front of the message.
⍝ Expects the Global `G` to be around which holds `AppLogTie`.
⍝ There is no ⍺: unlike `Log` this one does not need a server instance. It needs no trap
⍝ around it either - `AppLog` traps for itself, so that logging can never bring down
⍝ whatever was trying to report a problem.
 r←##.Plodder.AppLogError msg
⍝Done
